@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Decreto-Lei 4.657/1942 (LINDB), arts. 20 to 30 (added by Lei 13.655/2018): how public bodies and courts decide, and what binds them.
-- These articles are mostly duties to consider something, and permissions. A predicate named "... is breached by" is TRUE when the
-- article's duty or prohibition is broken and FALSE when it is not; FALSE never says the decision is otherwise lawful. A predicate named
-- "allows" is TRUE when the article gives the permission and FALSE when this article does not give it (not: forbids it).
-- The three spheres the articles name (administrative, controlling, judicial) are not an input: no rule here turns on which of the three
-- a decision belongs to, so the predicates are meant to be asked only about decisions in them.
-- Standards the text leaves to the decider ("proportional", "equitable", "efficient", "abnormal or excessive", "indispensable") are
-- booleans the caller supplies; nothing here decides whether a given decision meets them.

§ `LINDB arts. 20 to 30: deciding in public law`

§§ `Art. 20: abstract legal values`

-- src:68 | Art. 20. Nas esferas administrativa, controladora e judicial, não se decidirá com base em valores jurídicos abstratos sem que sejam consideradas as consequências práticas da decisão.
-- src:69 | Parágrafo único. A motivação demonstrará a necessidade e a adequação da medida imposta ou da invalidação de ato, contrato, ajuste, processo ou norma administrativa, inclusive em face das possíveis alternativas.
@ref LINDB art. 20 caput, sole paragraph (src:68-69)
GIVEN `the decision is based on abstract legal values` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practical consequences of the decision were considered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 20 caput is breached by a decision where` `the decision is based on abstract legal values` `the practical consequences of the decision were considered` MEANS
        `the decision is based on abstract legal values`
    AND NOT `the practical consequences of the decision were considered`

-- The motivation shows the necessity and the adequacy of the measure imposed, or of the invalidation, "including in face of the possible
-- alternatives". The last words are read as requiring the alternatives to be addressed too (fork F-20).
@ref LINDB art. 20 sole paragraph (src:69)
GIVEN `the motivation demonstrates the necessity of the measure or invalidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the motivation demonstrates the adequacy of the measure or invalidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the motivation addresses the possible alternatives` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 20 sole paragraph is met by a motivation where` `the motivation demonstrates the necessity of the measure or invalidation` `the motivation demonstrates the adequacy of the measure or invalidation` `the motivation addresses the possible alternatives` MEANS
        `the motivation demonstrates the necessity of the measure or invalidation`
    AND `the motivation demonstrates the adequacy of the measure or invalidation`
    AND `the motivation addresses the possible alternatives`

§§ `Art. 21: the consequences of an invalidation`

-- src:71 | Art. 21. A decisão que, nas esferas administrativa, controladora ou judicial, decretar a invalidação de ato, contrato, ajuste, processo ou norma administrativa deverá indicar de modo expresso suas consequências jurídicas e administrativas.
-- src:72 | Parágrafo único. A decisão a que se refere o caput deste artigo deverá, quando for o caso, indicar as condições para que a regularização ocorra de modo proporcional e equânime e sem prejuízo aos interesses gerais, não se podendo impor aos sujeitos atingidos ônus ou perdas que, em função das peculiaridades do caso, sejam anormais ou excessivos.
@ref LINDB art. 21 caput, sole paragraph (src:71-72)
GIVEN `the decision decrees the invalidation of an act, contract, adjustment, process or administrative norm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision expressly indicates its legal consequences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision expressly indicates its administrative consequences` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 21 caput is breached by a decision where` `the decision decrees the invalidation of an act, contract, adjustment, process or administrative norm` `the decision expressly indicates its legal consequences` `the decision expressly indicates its administrative consequences` MEANS
        `the decision decrees the invalidation of an act, contract, adjustment, process or administrative norm`
    AND (   NOT `the decision expressly indicates its legal consequences`
         OR NOT `the decision expressly indicates its administrative consequences`)

-- The sole paragraph: where the case calls for it, the decision indicates the conditions for a proportional and equitable regularisation,
-- and cannot put on those affected a burden or loss that, given the peculiarities of the case, is abnormal or excessive.
@ref LINDB art. 21 sole paragraph (src:72)
GIVEN `the decision decrees the invalidation of an act, contract, adjustment, process or administrative norm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case calls for conditions of regularisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision indicates the conditions for a proportional and equitable regularisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision puts on those affected a burden or loss that is abnormal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision puts on those affected a burden or loss that is excessive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 21 sole paragraph is breached by a decision where` `the decision decrees the invalidation of an act, contract, adjustment, process or administrative norm` `the case calls for conditions of regularisation` `the decision indicates the conditions for a proportional and equitable regularisation` `the decision puts on those affected a burden or loss that is abnormal` `the decision puts on those affected a burden or loss that is excessive` MEANS
        `the decision decrees the invalidation of an act, contract, adjustment, process or administrative norm`
    AND (   (`the case calls for conditions of regularisation` AND NOT `the decision indicates the conditions for a proportional and equitable regularisation`)
         OR `the decision puts on those affected a burden or loss that is abnormal`
         OR `the decision puts on those affected a burden or loss that is excessive`)

§§ `Art. 22: the real difficulties of the manager`

-- src:73 | Art. 22. Na interpretação de normas sobre gestão pública, serão considerados os obstáculos e as dificuldades reais do gestor e as exigências das políticas públicas a seu cargo, sem prejuízo dos direitos dos administrados.
-- src:74 | § 1º Em decisão sobre regularidade de conduta ou validade de ato, contrato, ajuste, processo ou norma administrativa, serão consideradas as circunstâncias práticas que houverem imposto, limitado ou condicionado a ação do agente.
-- src:76 | § 2º Na aplicação de sanções, serão consideradas a natureza e a gravidade da infração cometida, os danos que dela provierem para a administração pública, as circunstâncias agravantes ou atenuantes e os antecedentes do agente.
-- src:77 | § 3º As sanções aplicadas ao agente serão levadas em conta na dosimetria das demais sanções de mesma natureza e relativas ao mesmo fato.
@ref LINDB art. 22 caput to par. 3 (src:73-77)
GIVEN `the norm is about public management` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the manager's real obstacles and difficulties were considered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demands of the public policies in the manager's charge were considered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interpretation prejudices the rights of the administered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 22 caput is breached by an interpretation where` `the norm is about public management` `the manager's real obstacles and difficulties were considered` `the demands of the public policies in the manager's charge were considered` `the interpretation prejudices the rights of the administered` MEANS
        `the norm is about public management`
    AND (   NOT `the manager's real obstacles and difficulties were considered`
         OR NOT `the demands of the public policies in the manager's charge were considered`
         OR `the interpretation prejudices the rights of the administered`)

@ref LINDB art. 22 par. 1 (src:74)
GIVEN `the decision is on the regularity of conduct or the validity of an act, contract, adjustment, process or administrative norm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practical circumstances that imposed, limited or conditioned the agent's action were considered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 22 par. 1 is breached by a decision where` `the decision is on the regularity of conduct or the validity of an act, contract, adjustment, process or administrative norm` `the practical circumstances that imposed, limited or conditioned the agent's action were considered` MEANS
        `the decision is on the regularity of conduct or the validity of an act, contract, adjustment, process or administrative norm`
    AND NOT `the practical circumstances that imposed, limited or conditioned the agent's action were considered`

-- Par. 2: the four things to be considered in applying a sanction are read as all required (the list is a list of what is considered, not of grounds).
@ref LINDB art. 22 par. 2 (src:76)
GIVEN `a sanction is being applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the nature of the infraction was considered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the gravity of the infraction was considered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the damage to the public administration was considered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggravating or attenuating circumstances were considered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agent's antecedents were considered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 22 par. 2 is breached by the application of a sanction where` `a sanction is being applied` `the nature of the infraction was considered` `the gravity of the infraction was considered` `the damage to the public administration was considered` `the aggravating or attenuating circumstances were considered` `the agent's antecedents were considered` MEANS
        `a sanction is being applied`
    AND (   NOT `the nature of the infraction was considered`
         OR NOT `the gravity of the infraction was considered`
         OR NOT `the damage to the public administration was considered`
         OR NOT `the aggravating or attenuating circumstances were considered`
         OR NOT `the agent's antecedents were considered`)

-- Par. 3: sanctions already applied to the agent are counted in the dosimetry of the other sanctions of the same nature and for the same fact.
@ref LINDB art. 22 par. 3 (src:77)
GIVEN `the other sanction is of the same nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other sanction relates to the same fact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sanctions already applied to the agent were taken into account in its dosimetry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 22 par. 3 is breached by the dosimetry of a sanction where` `the other sanction is of the same nature` `the other sanction relates to the same fact` `the sanctions already applied to the agent were taken into account in its dosimetry` MEANS
        `the other sanction is of the same nature`
    AND `the other sanction relates to the same fact`
    AND NOT `the sanctions already applied to the agent were taken into account in its dosimetry`

§§ `Art. 23: a new interpretation and the transition`

-- src:79 | Art. 23. A decisão administrativa, controladora ou judicial que estabelecer interpretação ou orientação nova sobre norma de conteúdo indeterminado, impondo novo dever ou novo condicionamento de direito, deverá prever regime de transição quando indispensável para que o novo dever ou condicionamento de direito seja cumprido de modo proporcional, equânime e eficiente e sem prejuízo aos interesses gerais.
-- src:80 | Parágrafo único. (VETADO).
@ref LINDB art. 23 caput, sole paragraph (src:79-80)
GIVEN `the decision establishes a new interpretation or orientation on a norm of indeterminate content` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it imposes a new duty or a new conditioning of a right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a transition regime is indispensable for the duty or conditioning to be fulfilled proportionally, equitably and efficiently and without prejudice to the general interests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision provides a transition regime` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 23 caput is breached by a decision where` `the decision establishes a new interpretation or orientation on a norm of indeterminate content` `it imposes a new duty or a new conditioning of a right` `a transition regime is indispensable for the duty or conditioning to be fulfilled proportionally, equitably and efficiently and without prejudice to the general interests` `the decision provides a transition regime` MEANS
        `the decision establishes a new interpretation or orientation on a norm of indeterminate content`
    AND `it imposes a new duty or a new conditioning of a right`
    AND `a transition regime is indispensable for the duty or conditioning to be fulfilled proportionally, equitably and efficiently and without prejudice to the general interests`
    AND NOT `the decision provides a transition regime`

§§ `Art. 24: reviewing a completed act`

-- src:81 | Art. 24. A revisão, nas esferas administrativa, controladora ou judicial, quanto à validade de ato, contrato, ajuste, processo ou norma administrativa cuja produção já se houver completado levará em conta as orientações gerais da época, sendo vedado que, com base em mudança posterior de orientação geral, se declarem inválidas situações plenamente constituídas.
-- src:82 | Parágrafo único. Consideram-se orientações gerais as interpretações e especificações contidas em atos públicos de caráter geral ou em jurisprudência judicial ou administrativa majoritária, e ainda as adotadas por prática administrativa reiterada e de amplo conhecimento público.
@ref LINDB art. 24 caput, sole paragraph (src:81-82)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`art. 24 caput speaks of a later change and gives no moment of the day` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 24 caput forbids declaring invalid on the strength of a later change of general orientation, and the text gives no moment of the day to say whether a change on the very day the production was completed is later"

-- The prohibition: a situation fully constituted may not be declared invalid on the strength of a later change of general orientation,
-- where the production of the act has already been completed. The production day is NOTHING when it has not been completed.
-- "Later" is read as strictly later; the day the production was completed is refused, for want of a moment of the day.
@ref LINDB art. 24 caput (src:81)
GIVEN `the day the production of the act was completed` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the general orientation changed` IS A DATE
      `the declaration of invalidity rests on the change of general orientation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the situation was fully constituted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 24 caput forbids declaring the situation invalid where` `the day the production of the act was completed` `and` `the day the general orientation changed` `the declaration of invalidity rests on the change of general orientation` `the situation was fully constituted` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the production of the act was completed`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST produced THEN
        IF (NOT `the declaration of invalidity rests on the change of general orientation`) OR (NOT `the situation was fully constituted`)
        THEN FALSE
        ELSE
            BRANCH
                IF `the day the general orientation changed` GREATER THAN produced THEN TRUE
                IF `the day the general orientation changed` LESS THAN produced THEN FALSE
                OTHERWISE `art. 24 caput speaks of a later change and gives no moment of the day`

-- The review takes into account the general orientations of the time.
@ref LINDB art. 24 caput (src:81)
GIVEN `the production of the act has already been completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the review took into account the general orientations of the time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 24 caput is breached by a review where` `the production of the act has already been completed` `the review took into account the general orientations of the time` MEANS
    `the production of the act has already been completed` AND NOT `the review took into account the general orientations of the time`

-- The sole paragraph lists what counts as a general orientation. "e ainda" (and also) is read as adding a third kind, not as making the
-- kinds cumulative (fork F-24); the third kind needs both repetition and wide public knowledge.
@ref LINDB art. 24 sole paragraph (src:82)
GIVEN `it is an interpretation or specification contained in a public act of general character` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an interpretation or specification contained in majority judicial or administrative jurisprudence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an interpretation or specification adopted by repeated administrative practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that practice is of wide public knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is a general orientation under art. 24 sole paragraph` `it is an interpretation or specification contained in a public act of general character` `it is an interpretation or specification contained in majority judicial or administrative jurisprudence` `it is an interpretation or specification adopted by repeated administrative practice` `that practice is of wide public knowledge` MEANS
        `it is an interpretation or specification contained in a public act of general character`
     OR `it is an interpretation or specification contained in majority judicial or administrative jurisprudence`
     OR (   `it is an interpretation or specification adopted by repeated administrative practice`
        AND `that practice is of wide public knowledge`)

§§ `Art. 25: vetoed`

-- src:83 | Art. 25. (VETADO).

§§ `Art. 26: the compromise`

-- src:84 | Art. 26. Para eliminar irregularidade, incerteza jurídica ou situação contenciosa na aplicação do direito público, inclusive no caso de expedição de licença, a autoridade administrativa poderá, após oitiva do órgão jurídico e, quando for o caso, após realização de consulta pública, e presentes razões de relevante interesse geral, celebrar compromisso com os interessados, observada a legislação aplicável, o qual só produzirá efeitos a partir de sua publicação oficial.
-- src:86 | § 1º O compromisso referido no caput deste artigo:
-- src:88 | I - buscará solução jurídica proporcional, equânime, eficiente e compatível com os interesses gerais;
-- src:89 | II – (VETADO);
-- src:90 | III - não poderá conferir desoneração permanente de dever ou condicionamento de direito reconhecidos por orientação geral;
-- src:91 | IV - deverá prever com clareza as obrigações das partes, o prazo para seu cumprimento e as sanções aplicáveis em caso de descumprimento.
-- src:92 | § 2º (VETADO).
@ref LINDB art. 26 caput to par. 2 (src:84-92)
GIVEN `the purpose is to eliminate an irregularity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is to eliminate a legal uncertainty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is to eliminate a contentious situation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legal organ was heard` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a public consultation is called for in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a public consultation was held` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasons of relevant general interest are present` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the compromise observes the applicable legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 26 caput allows the administrative authority to conclude a compromise where` `the purpose is to eliminate an irregularity` `the purpose is to eliminate a legal uncertainty` `the purpose is to eliminate a contentious situation` `the legal organ was heard` `a public consultation is called for in the case` `a public consultation was held` `reasons of relevant general interest are present` `the compromise observes the applicable legislation` MEANS
        (   `the purpose is to eliminate an irregularity`
         OR `the purpose is to eliminate a legal uncertainty`
         OR `the purpose is to eliminate a contentious situation`)
    AND `the legal organ was heard`
    AND ((NOT `a public consultation is called for in the case`) OR `a public consultation was held`)
    AND `reasons of relevant general interest are present`
    AND `the compromise observes the applicable legislation`

-- Par. 1, III and IV. Item I ("will seek a proportional, equitable, efficient solution compatible with the general interests") states an aim
-- with no test and is not a predicate (see NOTES.md); item II is vetoed.
@ref LINDB art. 26 par. 1, III and IV (src:90-91)
GIVEN `it confers a permanent exoneration from a duty or conditioning of a right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the duty or conditioning was recognised by a general orientation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides clearly the obligations of the parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides the deadline for compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides the sanctions applicable on non-compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 26 par. 1 is breached by a compromise where` `it confers a permanent exoneration from a duty or conditioning of a right` `the duty or conditioning was recognised by a general orientation` `it provides clearly the obligations of the parties` `it provides the deadline for compliance` `it provides the sanctions applicable on non-compliance` MEANS
        (   `it confers a permanent exoneration from a duty or conditioning of a right`
        AND `the duty or conditioning was recognised by a general orientation`)
     OR NOT `it provides clearly the obligations of the parties`
     OR NOT `it provides the deadline for compliance`
     OR NOT `it provides the sanctions applicable on non-compliance`

@ref LINDB art. 26 caput (src:84)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`art. 26 caput gives no moment of the day of the official publication` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 26 caput says the compromise produces effects from its official publication and the text gives no moment of the day of publication"

-- The compromise produces effects from its official publication: effects begin at some moment of the publication day (so from that day on, in the weak sense),
-- and are in force throughout only from the next day. On the day itself the second is refused (fork F-26).
@ref LINDB art. 26 caput (src:84)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the day of the official publication of the compromise` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the compromise produces effects at some moment of` d `from its official publication on` `the day of the official publication of the compromise` MEANS
    d AT LEAST `the day of the official publication of the compromise`

@ref LINDB art. 26 caput (src:84)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the day of the official publication of the compromise` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the compromise produces effects throughout` d `from its official publication on` `the day of the official publication of the compromise` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF d LESS THAN `the day of the official publication of the compromise` THEN FALSE
        IF d GREATER THAN `the day of the official publication of the compromise` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE `art. 26 caput gives no moment of the day of the official publication`

§§ `Art. 27: compensation`

-- src:93 | Art. 27. A decisão do processo, nas esferas administrativa, controladora ou judicial, poderá impor compensação por benefícios indevidos ou prejuízos anormais ou injustos resultantes do processo ou da conduta dos envolvidos.
-- src:94 | § 1º A decisão sobre a compensação será motivada, ouvidas previamente as partes sobre seu cabimento, sua forma e, se for o caso, seu valor.
-- src:95 | § 2º Para prevenir ou regular a compensação, poderá ser celebrado compromisso processual entre os envolvidos.
@ref LINDB art. 27 caput to par. 2 (src:93-95)
GIVEN `there are undue benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are abnormal losses` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are unjust losses` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they result from the process or from the conduct of those involved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 27 caput allows the decision to impose compensation where` `there are undue benefits` `there are abnormal losses` `there are unjust losses` `they result from the process or from the conduct of those involved` MEANS
        (`there are undue benefits` OR `there are abnormal losses` OR `there are unjust losses`)
    AND `they result from the process or from the conduct of those involved`

-- Par. 1: the decision on compensation is reasoned, the parties having been heard beforehand on whether it is due, its form and, where the
-- case arises, its value.
@ref LINDB art. 27 par. 1 (src:94)
GIVEN `the decision on compensation is reasoned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties were heard beforehand on whether compensation is due` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties were heard beforehand on its form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its value is in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties were heard beforehand on its value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 27 par. 1 is met by a decision on compensation where` `the decision on compensation is reasoned` `the parties were heard beforehand on whether compensation is due` `the parties were heard beforehand on its form` `its value is in question` `the parties were heard beforehand on its value` MEANS
        `the decision on compensation is reasoned`
    AND `the parties were heard beforehand on whether compensation is due`
    AND `the parties were heard beforehand on its form`
    AND ((NOT `its value is in question`) OR `the parties were heard beforehand on its value`)

@ref LINDB art. 27 par. 2 (src:95)
GIVEN `the purpose is to prevent or regulate compensation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made between those involved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 27 par. 2 allows a procedural compromise where` `the purpose is to prevent or regulate compensation` `it is made between those involved` MEANS
    `the purpose is to prevent or regulate compensation` AND `it is made between those involved`

§§ `Art. 28: the personal liability of the public agent`

-- src:96 | Art. 28. O agente público responderá pessoalmente por suas decisões ou opiniões técnicas em caso de dolo ou erro grosseiro.
-- src:97 | § 1º (VETADO).
-- src:98 | § 2º (VETADO).
-- src:99 | § 3º (VETADO).
@ref LINDB art. 28 caput to par. 3 (src:96-99)
GIVEN `it is a decision or technical opinion of a public agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is intent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is gross error` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the public agent answers personally on a ground listed in art. 28 caput where` `it is a decision or technical opinion of a public agent` `there is intent` `there is gross error` MEANS
    `it is a decision or technical opinion of a public agent` AND (`there is intent` OR `there is gross error`)

§§ `Art. 29: public consultation on normative acts`

-- src:100 | Art. 29. Em qualquer órgão ou Poder, a edição de atos normativos por autoridade administrativa, salvo os de mera organização interna, poderá ser precedida de consulta pública para manifestação de interessados, preferencialmente por meio eletrônico, a qual será considerada na decisão.
-- src:102 | § 1º A convocação conterá a minuta do ato normativo e fixará o prazo e demais condições da consulta pública, observadas as normas legais e regulamentares específicas, se houver.
-- src:104 | § 2º (VETADO).
@ref LINDB art. 29 caput to par. 2 (src:100-104)
GIVEN `the act is a normative act issued by an administrative authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is of mere internal organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 29 caput allows a public consultation before the act where` `the act is a normative act issued by an administrative authority` `the act is of mere internal organisation` MEANS
    `the act is a normative act issued by an administrative authority` AND NOT `the act is of mere internal organisation`

-- A consultation that was held "will be considered in the decision".
@ref LINDB art. 29 caput (src:100)
GIVEN `a public consultation was held` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consultation was considered in the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 29 caput is breached by a decision where` `a public consultation was held` `the consultation was considered in the decision` MEANS
    `a public consultation was held` AND NOT `the consultation was considered in the decision`

@ref LINDB art. 29 par. 1 (src:102)
GIVEN `the convocation contains the draft of the normative act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the convocation fixes the deadline of the consultation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the convocation fixes the other conditions of the consultation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 29 par. 1 is met by a convocation where` `the convocation contains the draft of the normative act` `the convocation fixes the deadline of the consultation` `the convocation fixes the other conditions of the consultation` MEANS
        `the convocation contains the draft of the normative act`
    AND `the convocation fixes the deadline of the consultation`
    AND `the convocation fixes the other conditions of the consultation`

§§ `Art. 30: legal security`

-- src:106 | Art. 30. As autoridades públicas devem atuar para aumentar a segurança jurídica na aplicação das normas, inclusive por meio de regulamentos, súmulas administrativas e respostas a consultas.
-- src:107 | Parágrafo único. Os instrumentos previstos no caput deste artigo terão caráter vinculante em relação ao órgão ou entidade a que se destinam, até ulterior revisão.
@ref LINDB art. 30 caput, sole paragraph (src:106-107)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`art. 30 sole paragraph speaks only of the organ or entity an instrument is directed to` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 30 sole paragraph says the instruments bind the organ or entity they are directed to and says nothing of any other"

@ref LINDB art. 30 sole paragraph (src:107)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`art. 30 sole paragraph speaks of instruments the caput provides and the text does not say whether it means only those named` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 30 caput names regulations, administrative precedents and answers to consultations 'inclusive', and the text does not say whether other instruments are 'provided for in the caput'"

@ref LINDB art. 30 sole paragraph (src:107)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`art. 30 sole paragraph gives no moment of the day of the revision` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 30 sole paragraph binds until further revision and the text gives no moment of the day of the revision"

-- "Until further revision": the instrument binds on days before the revision and not on days after it. The revision day is NOTHING while
-- there has been none; on the revision day itself the text does not say whether the earlier instrument still binds.
@ref LINDB art. 30 sole paragraph (src:107)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the day the instrument was revised` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an instrument binds on` d `until a revision on` `the day the instrument was revised` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the instrument was revised`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST revised THEN
        BRANCH
            IF d LESS THAN revised THEN TRUE
            IF d GREATER THAN revised THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE `art. 30 sole paragraph gives no moment of the day of the revision`

-- The instrument binds the organ or entity it is directed to, and the text says nothing of any other.
@ref LINDB art. 30 sole paragraph (src:107)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the instrument is one the caput names` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the organ or entity is the one the instrument is directed to` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the instrument was revised` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an instrument of art. 30 caput binds, on` d `, where` `the instrument is one the caput names` `the organ or entity is the one the instrument is directed to` `the day the instrument was revised` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the instrument is one the caput names`
        THEN `art. 30 sole paragraph speaks of instruments the caput provides and the text does not say whether it means only those named`
        IF NOT `the organ or entity is the one the instrument is directed to`
        THEN `art. 30 sole paragraph speaks only of the organ or entity an instrument is directed to`
        OTHERWISE `an instrument binds on` d `until a revision on` `the day the instrument was revised`
